## Third-party Content

This project fetches and builds the following third-party content, which is
**not** covered by the Apache-2.0 license declared above.

mke2fs (e2fsprogs) (1.47.4)

* License: GPL-2.0-only AND LGPL-2.0-only AND BSD-3-Clause AND MIT
* Project: https://github.com/tytso/e2fsprogs
* Source: https://github.com/tytso/e2fsprogs/archive/refs/tags/v1.47.4.tar.gz

The `ext4` rule's toolchain builds the `mke2fs` executable from the e2fsprogs
source tree (fetched by the `e2fsprogs` repository rule, see
`rules/linux/tools/e2fsprogs.bzl`) and uses it only as a build-time tool to
format generated filesystem images; no e2fsprogs source or object code is
linked into, or distributed as part of, this project's own Apache-2.0
licensed targets. Per upstream's own `NOTICE`, e2fsprogs is GPL-2.0-only
except for `lib/ext2fs`/`lib/e2p` (LGPL-2.0-only), `lib/uuid` (BSD-3-Clause,
see `lib/uuid/COPYING`), and `lib/et`/`lib/ss` (MIT). Because the built
`mke2fs` binary links code from all of these, the executable as a whole is
governed by GPL-2.0-only. The generated `mke2fs` build (see
`templates/linux/tools/e2fsprogs/mke2fs.BUILD.template`) exposes the
upstream `NOTICE` and `lib/uuid/COPYING` license texts via a public
`license_files` filegroup; anyone redistributing a built `mke2fs` binary is
responsible for carrying these notices, and a corresponding source offer,
along with it.

Every compiled target in that BUILD file is tagged `no-cache`,
`no-remote-cache`, and `no-remote-exec`, so its compile/link outputs are
never written to a Bazel disk cache or remote cache. Consumers should still
ensure their own CI caches Bazel's `--disk_cache`/`--remote_cache` paths
specifically, rather than the raw build output tree (e.g. the whole
`~/.cache/bazel` output-user-root) — caching the latter would bypass these
tags and could incidentally distribute built GPL-2.0 binaries to anyone able
to restore that cache (e.g. via a pull request).

